What I actually measured (all read-only, minutes of CPU): rotation damage per archive is −6.6pp on small RealTalk archives vs −23.1pp on large ones — with RT04 *gaining* +7pp from random rotation, which falsifies any universal "axes are meaningful" claim; a float-with-qscale-weights scorer I built to attack the bottleneck diagnosis scored 42.70 (below cosine's 48.51), so that attack failed honestly; the IDF rare-band gain survives single-archive removal but flips sign across archives (+12.8 to −8.4) and is null under the sym scorer; and 52% of scorer-failures have gold outside the top-100 pool, unfixable by any reranker.

